        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "If using salt cod, soak overnight in cold water, changing the water twice."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Boil potato until completely tender. Drain and mash until smooth."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Poach cod in simmering water for 8 to 10 minutes until it flakes easily."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Drain cod. Flake the flesh, removing all skin and bones."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Combine mashed potato and flaked cod in a large bowl."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Slowly beat in the olive oil with a wooden spoon, a little at a time."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add warm milk to loosen the mixture to a spreadable consistency."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Stir in garlic, lemon juice, and parsley. Season. Serve warm with toasted bread or raw vegetables."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Mixture is grainy",
              "cause": "Oil added too fast or cod was overcooked",
              "fix": "Beat more vigorously and add a little more warm milk."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Too salty",
              "cause": "Salt cod not soaked long enough",
              "fix": "Add more potato and lemon juice to balance the salt."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Stiff and dry",
              "cause": "Not enough liquid",
              "fix": "Add warm milk a tablespoon at a time until the texture loosens."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Brandade has been made in the south of France for centuries. Salt cod arrived via Basque and Portuguese traders who fished the North Atlantic. The dish spread inland because dried cod kept well before refrigeration. In Nimes it is sometimes made without potato, which is considered the purer version. It is eaten on Fridays and during Lent in traditional households."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}